<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#cccccc"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST3357"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->J<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->J<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->12-2004<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Monday, January 03, 2005 - 10:48 pm: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->Pax56: Do I get .25 points at least? <BR> <BR>Perhaps BTK&#39;s first name is Ben &#40;as in the pet rat in the movie &#34;Willard&#34;&#41;.<!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 3357-->
<!--Post: 3358--><!--Time: 1104821997-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#f7f7f7"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST3358"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Armchairpi<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Armchairpi<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->12-2004<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Monday, January 03, 2005 - 10:59 pm: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->brainstorming here... perhaps &#34;petra&#34; and &#34;tina&#34; are not from btk at all, but a world puzzle created by wpd to encode a message to btk within the recent press release? <BR> <BR>which, naturally, means there could be even more still left to find in the press release....<!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 3358-->
<!--Post: 3360--><!--Time: 1104823005-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#cccccc"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST3360"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Pax56<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Pax56<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->12-2004<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Monday, January 03, 2005 - 11:16 pm: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->&#40;lol&#41; J - at least .25 in my book, maybe a full one!  More than I deserve. <BR> <BR>I&#39;m ashamed to admit - when I first saw it on the way into the site, I looked at it briefly and said to myself &#34;Hey, that looks like Petra and Tina.  I wonder if Tom knows that?&#34;  Yeah.  Uh-huh.   <BR> <BR>Seriously, kids remember which of their friends owned pet rats - it&#39;s the kind of thing you don&#39;t forget &#40;at least, I didn&#39;t&#41;.  If BTK had any friends at all, somebody is going to remember.  Maybe the joke is on him now. <BR> <BR>Armchair - You may be right - I never considered it could be a 2-way thing.  I would actually love to see &#40;if it exists&#41; BTK&#39;s actual statement about Petra and Tina.  The context would probably confirm if it was really a joke.  Otherwise you&#39;re right, there could even be games going on in the released info.  But.... <BR> <BR>Sorry - wife says &#34;Go to bed!&#34;  More later.....<!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 3360-->
<!--Post: 3366--><!--Time: 1104827441-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#f7f7f7"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST3366"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Jujuree<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Jujuree<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->12-2004<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Tuesday, January 04, 2005 - 12:30 am: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->Thanks for the link, Pax.  I have AOL and often times when a site makes a change, my browser won&#39;t show me the change for a day or two, so I still can&#39;t see it at index.html. <BR> <BR>That is very interesting.  I wonder if BTK did have a pet rat?  I know a lot of people here felt there was something screwy with all that Petra/Tina stuff. <BR> <BR>Maybe a pet rat named Tina?  When I think &#34;Petra Tina&#34; together, with the word &#34;rat&#34; in mind, it sounds like &#34;pet rat tina.&#34;  The double t&#39;s run together as one. <BR> <BR>Hopefully, the rat in the cage will soon be BTK himself, sitting in the pokey.<!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 3366-->
<!--Post: 3764--><!--Time: 1105199362-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#cccccc"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST3764"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Thinker<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Thinker<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->12-2004<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Saturday, January 08, 2005 - 7:49 am: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->Perhaps BTK felt the &#34;pet rat in a&#34; metaphor was simply his viewing of his victims as his rat.  It may not be actual at all.  With his love of word games, a metaphorical aspect would not be unlikely.<!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 3764-->
<!--Post: 3855--><!--Time: 1105330404-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#f7f7f7"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST3855"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Q<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Q<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->12-2004<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Sunday, January 09, 2005 - 8:13 pm: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->Actually... The original movie &#34;Willard&#34; had a sequel called &#34;Ben&#34;... <BR> <BR>...but no need to bring Michael Jackson into it...yikes!<!--/Text--></td></tr>
